From 555d0e31605275e76ee4c013f2231d8beabf8894 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pento95 <173375476+Pento95@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 05:39:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [hyperinkling] Inkling 2 Mini on Ampere (sm86)

Runs Inkling2Loop on RTX 3090-class GPUs (on top of vllm#69165, which
gates PDL/TMA, e4m3 conversions and the native conv/mix kernels below SM90):
- sm8x takes the SM12x Triton path (use_sm12x_path): Triton relative
  attention and the SM12x low-M bf16 GEMMs (ll_gemm_sm120).
- Routed experts on Marlin MoE (ops/moe_marlin.py): NVFP4, MXFP8 and
  HyperInkling INT4 (AWQ layout, g128 asym, quant format "int4_awq").
- INT8 W8A16 Triton linears (ops/linear_w8.py) for attention, LM head
  (fp32 logits) and token embeddings (optionally in pinned host RAM, UVA),
  behind HYPERINKLING_{ATTN,HEAD,EMBED}_W8 / HYPERINKLING_EMBED_UVA; tiles
  by output width (k/v, o, qkvr, LM head) for decode and verify batches
  (1-128 rows).
- E4M3 KV decode on sm8x as fp16 holding value * 2^-8 (e4m3_f16_scaled):
  the 2^8 goes into the softmax scale and the output, fp16 MMAs.
- sconv conv-state cache backs only each step's tail (SconvStateManager,
  after DFlashSlidingWindowManager): the window, the drafts in flight and
  one hit alignment; the rest of a prefill chunk is null and the conv skips
  stores into the null block; the window below the request's
  shared-prefix junction is backed too (note_shared_prefix).
- Marlin MoE rows in ascending order per expert (order_rows,
  HYPERINKLING_MOE_ORDER, default on): moe_align_block_size leaves them in
  atomic order, and a row's result depends on its Marlin block.
- Decode attention of the full layers: at least two CTAs per SM (21 splits
  at one request instead of 10), +3% decode at 32k, +10% at 128k.
- Loop controllers and sconv dynamic taps on Triton GEMVs (ops/bgemv.py,
  split-K down projection, up to 64 rows) instead of cuBLAS wmma kernels at
  decode and verify sizes.
- Image dummy size follows --limit-mm-per-prompt width/height up to
  4096 px, so pages above 2048 px fit the encoder budget instead of
  waiting forever.
- Calibration capture hook (HYPERINKLING_CAPTURE_DIR) for GPTQ.
- Images over the profiled page (HYPERINKLING_IMAGE_MAX_CELLS, 40 px cells)
  or over the model's 4096 px per side are scaled down (bicubic, aspect
  kept) in the processor instead of waiting forever.
- HYPERINKLING_VISION_HOST=1: the vision tower's weights in pinned host
  RAM, copied to the GPU layer by layer around each layer's forward.
- DSpark drafter: base logits and the Markov fold from the shared INT8 LM
  head (the bf16 head is no longer kept); the fold in INT4/INT8
  (HYPERINKLING_DSPARK_FOLD=w4|w8); draft layers in INT4 g128 RTN on a
  Triton W4A16 kernel (ops/linear_w4.py, HYPERINKLING_DRAFT_W4; split-K below
  16k output columns, one launch above);
  Markov embedding in pinned host RAM with HYPERINKLING_EMBED_UVA; RoPE
  angles computed in-kernel (no cos/sin table growing with max_model_len,
  so --max-model-len -1 costs nothing); draft
  KV as the target's unit-scale E4M3 (HYPERINKLING_DRAFT_KV_FP8, through a
  KV-write-only FlashAttention impl: the draft's attention runs in
  block_decode_attention).
- DFlash2 drafts (incoai/Inkling-2-Mini-DFlash2): the Inkling2 DFlash2
  speculator of our upstream PR (capture ids as-is, the target's embed_norm,
  selector_softcap_mode); on sm8x the draft's attention runs in
  block_decode_attention (full CUDA graphs; FlashInfer, chosen for the fp8
  cache, has none), the shared INT8 head goes through Inkling2LogitsProcessor
  and the draft linears are INT4 g128 (HYPERINKLING_DRAFT_W4); the context
  lookup too (its point masses claimed in DFlash2's sparse draft-logits cache).
- The INT8 LM head computes the real vocabulary's rows only.
- Online verify length for dynamic speculative decoding
  (v1/spec_decode/dynamic/adaptive_k.py, HYPERINKLING_SPEC_ADAPTIVE): the
  length with the most expected tokens per ms, from decayed per-position
  acceptance and measured decode step times; decode graphs for every
  candidate length. A step that verified no draft leaves the acceptance as it
  was.
- Context lookup drafting (HYPERINKLING_LOOKUP=1, ops/lookup.py, after
  HyperQwen's dflash2-lookup-drafting): a suffix match of 8 tokens or more in
  the request's history replaces the DSpark drafts (a choice that never
  depends on them), point masses in the draft-logits cache keep rejection
  sampling exact; the token history is kept on the GPU while it is on.
- disable_any_whitespace also reaches structural tags, which is how Inkling's
  parser asks for JSON (the server-wide part of vllm#68990).
- Tool calls (parser/inkling.py): HYPERINKLING_TOOL_GRAMMAR=1 constrains each
  tool block to JSON, and to the parameter schemas when a tool is strict;
  reasoning and text stay free, except that a required or named tool_choice
  leaves only reasoning and calls, and parallel_tool_calls=false stops at one.
  Arguments after a misplaced brace are returned whole instead of cut there.
- Long streamed tool arguments without re-parsing them at every delta: the
  arg_value_extender of vllm#69297 (MedUnes), with its tests; merged in main,
  so it goes when BASE moves to main.
- Serving, after HyperQwen: --api-key guards every path but /health,
  /ping, /load, /version (auth-deny-default); stall sentinel
  (VLLM_ENGINE_STALL_SENTINEL_S, engine-stall-sentinel); continuous usage
  kept while a tool parser buffers deltas (continuous-stream-usage).
- Extensible KV cache sizing: HYPERINKLING_KV_KEEP_FREE_GIB keeps that much
  free after warmup (at least the measured activation peak) in place of the
  margin plus reserve (~3.25 GiB here).

